# NET-TELEPORT-VELOCITY: velocity and smoothing across a pawn teleport, on the own client and on the proxies.
# UE: the adjustment carries velocity (ClientAdjustPosition(TimeStamp, NewLoc, NewVel, ...)); the client keeps the
# newest acknowledged move (FNetworkPredictionData_Client_Character::LastAckedMove), so a later server verdict on it
# is read at the next exchange; a snapped mesh has its pose evaluated in that tick; LogNetPlayerMovement records
# every correction. Ours: the own client takes the server's whole state on a correction (Net/MovePrediction.cpp
# Reconcile) and keeps the last acked move (MovePredictor::m_LastAcked) - a re-acked step whose state the server
# changed is a correction named " (re-acked)"; a proxy across a teleport runs on along its earlier sample's velocity
# until the later sample's time, then cuts (Net/Replication.cpp InterpolationBuffer::Sample); the editor client marks
# a proxy's pose teleported at its cut and logs it (Engine/Net/ClientNetDriver.cpp); the bot logs each proxy cut
# with the sample's motion over the steps before it (Tools/DesertNetProbe --bot).
# Before this feature (scn-1127-084232): the at-rest teleport reached A 416 ms after the server's line (the re-acked
# step was dropped as Unknown); a proxy straddling a teleport was held at the old place with its old running
# velocity for the whole cut window; a proxy's cut kept the old place's pose/LOD for one frame; nothing logged a cut.
# Played by scripts/Dev/net_scenario.py. A's frames come from its pawn camera (--shot-player-view). A sprints +X for
# 600 m (server position); B is a bot standing at its spawn, so B's proxy of pawn 1 is 200-400 m away, in the 6 Hz
# band: the cut window is 167 ms, longer than the bot's ~100 ms measuring span.
# Net coordinates are Y-up (X, Y, Z), cm.
Мир Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce
# The spawn points are the ground (feet, cm): see NET-TELEPORT-ENCROACH.scn.
Роль server server --role all --source 0,0,0 --pawn assets:Prefabs/Pawn_Player.deprefab --spawn 0,-398,1150 --spawn 500,-427,-200 --steps 864000
Ждать server 60 \[Server\] listening on port
Роль A editor account=1 lag=75 loss=2 --play --shot-frames 100000 --shot-every 1 --shot-player-view --quality PostProcess.MotionBlurQuality=0 --net-walk-cm 60000 --net-walk-dir 1,0,0 --net-walk-mode sprint
Ждать A 1800 \[Net\] in session
Роль B bot account=2 lag=75 loss=2 --seconds 1500
Ждать server 120 player 2 \(account 2\): pawn net id 2 spawned
# A is 200+ m from B, sprinting at 965 cm/s.
Ждать server 120 player 1 account 1 \(2\d{4},
# 1. Sprint teleport - the velocity is the server's, on the own client and on the proxy.
# (40000, 300, 3000) is under the landscape (576 cm): the placer lifts the capsule onto the surface.
Консоль server teleport 1 40000 300 3000
Ждать server 120 player 1: pawn 1 teleported to \(40000, 5[6-9]\d, 3000\) cm
# The correction carries the server state one snapshot interval (up to ~13 input steps, 6 Hz band) after the landing:
# the pawn just past the destination, speed rebuilt at 34 cm/s per step - each component below 600 cm/s, never the sprint.
Ждать A 120 correction \d+ at input step \d+: the server has the own pawn at \(400\d\d\.\d, 5[6-9]\d\.\d, (?:29|30)\d\d\.\d\) cm.*beyond the smoothing distance.*v \(-?\d+, -?\d+, -?\d+\) \S+ vs server v \(-?(?:[0-5]?\d?\d), -?(?:[0-5]?\d?\d), -?(?:[0-5]?\d?\d)\)
Тогда A tp_sprint the frame of that correction tick from A's pawn camera: the landscape surface under the camera and the horizon in front at standing height - not the terrain's underside, not a void; the pawn is at the destination, not somewhere along its old sprint line
# The proxy's first post-teleport snapshot carries the server's post-landing velocity: no slide along 965 cm/s. That
# snapshot lands up to one snapshot interval (up to ~13 input steps) after the landing - the target just past the
# destination, speed rebuilt at 34 cm/s per step: each component below 600 cm/s, never the sprint.
Ждать B 120 \] pawn 1 teleport cut at t=\S+: sampled \(\S+, \S+, \S+\) -> \(400\d\d, 5[6-9]\d, 3000\) cm;.*the first snapshot of this teleport carried velocity \(-?(?:[0-5]?\d?\d), -?(?:[0-5]?\d?\d), -?(?:[0-5]?\d?\d)\) cm/s
# Over the ~100 ms before the cut the proxy's drawn displacement matches its locomotion speed (before: moved 0 vs
# ~96 cm accounted at a sprint - the proxy ran on the spot).
Запомнить moved B pawn 1 teleport cut .* the sample moved (-?\d+) cm,
Запомнить accounted B pawn 1 teleport cut .* accounts for (-?\d+) cm;
Сверить moved accounted 40
# 2. At-rest teleport - the own client learns it at the next snapshot. The scripted sprint ends (600 m of server
# position); one second at rest turns the stationary input rate on.
Ждать A 900 \[Net\] walked \d+ cm \(server position\): stopping
Ждать A 60 fresh 60x \[Shot\] recorded frame_
# Three teleports 0.7 s apart (not a multiple of the 0.5 s stationary period, so at least one lands in the idle half
# of the window). By the lines' own stamps each correction is <= 350 ms after its server line (lag 75 + a 33 ms ack +
# one ~200 ms shot frame; scn-1127-084232 measured 416 ms); at least one of the three correction lines carries
# " (re-acked)" - the acceptance agent reads both from A.log and server.log (a run where none does is repeated once;
